This project contains a modified copy of the backend of "Generative Agents"
by Joon Sung Park et al. (https://github.com/joonspk-research/generative_agents),
licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (see reverie/LICENSE-original-Apache-2.0).

Paper: Joon Sung Park, Joseph C. O'Brien, Carrie J. Cai, Meredith Ringel Morris,
Percy Liang, Michael S. Bernstein. "Generative Agents: Interactive Simulacra of
Human Behavior." UIST '23. https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.03442

Files under reverie/ are the authors' code. Changes made in this project:

  reverie/persona/prompt_template/gpt_structure.py
      Rewritten to call the current OpenAI SDK through reverie/llm_gateway.py
      (retired models replaced by one configurable chat model; completion
      prompts sent unchanged with a "continue the text" instruction; same
      temperature / max_tokens / stop; errors retried or stopped instead of
      returning "ChatGPT ERROR"). Function names and retry loops kept.
  reverie/llm_gateway.py        New: cache, cost tracking, budget, mock mode.
  reverie/utils.py              New: paths (the authors' file is not published).
  reverie/reverie.py            Headless: no Selenium / Phaser frontend; the
                                next environment file is written by the backend
                                exactly as the frontend did; resume in place;
                                movements logged to movement/movements.jsonl.
  reverie/persona/memory_structures/scratch.py
                                save() accepts an empty clock / no action yet.
  all reverie/*.py              bare `except:` changed to `except Exception:`
                                so stop signals are not swallowed.
  reverie/test.py               removed (needed a hard-coded API key).
  reverie/memory_fix.py         New: switches for our memory fixes (master's
                                contribution), all OFF by default; set with
                                `main.py ... --memory-fix A`.
  reverie/persona/cognitive_modules/retrieve.py
                                Fix A (only with --memory-fix A): recency =
                                decay ** game hours since last retrieved, as in
                                the paper (Sec. 4.1). The original decay **
                                (place in a list sorted oldest-first) is kept
                                as the default; it ignores time and gives the
                                most recently used memory the lowest score.

Files under frontend/ are the authors' environment/frontend_server (replay
viewer). Changes:

  frontend/frontend_server/settings/   Django 2.2 -> 6: no database, admin,
                                S3 storage or CORS; secret key generated at
                                start; art assets served from external/.
  frontend/frontend_server/urls.py     url() -> re_path(); only the replay routes.
  frontend/translator/views.py         demo and replay_persona_state kept
                                (logic unchanged, paths from settings); live
                                simulation views removed; landing lists replays.
  frontend/templates/                  {% load staticfiles %} -> {% load static %};
                                jQuery pinned and loaded before Bootstrap;
                                third-party visitor tracker removed; optional
                                ?renderer=canvas; landing page lists replays;
                                live-mode templates (home, path_tester) removed.
  The art assets (tilesets, character sprites) are not copied into this repo;
  `python main.py setup --viewer` downloads them from the authors' repository.
